IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P9-art-82-84: Article 82 "Compliant AI systems which present a risk", Article 83 "Formal non-compliance" and
-- Article 84 "Union AI testing support structures" (consolidated text of 27.7.2026; unchanged by the Omnibus).
-- Group General (2 August 2026). Each function takes `the date asked` first (and the AI system, for Articles 82 and 83);
-- before the group applies, or where Article 111(2) saves the system, the answer is NOTHING (limited by its own wording).
-- JUST FALSE is the text's own "no": a "where" condition of the paragraph that is not met (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)).
-- The market surveillance authorities, the Commission and the Member States are officials: they have no seat. What the
-- Articles mean to the operator (it must act on the authority's requirement; it must be consulted and told the Commission's
-- decision) and to the provider (it must be required to end a formal non-compliance) is asked in the seat modules.
-- "High-risk AI system" is the seam S1 (the route by which the AI system is high-risk): the AI system record carries it.
-- Seam S11 (Article 79): `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk`.

§ `Seam S14: the reference each provision gives to Article 2(2)`

-- Article 2(2): for a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in
-- Section B of Annex I, "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply". The keel asks of a provision by its Article
-- number, letter and paragraph; paragraph 0 would mean the whole Article. Each function below that is about an AI system asks it of its own paragraph.

`Art 82(1) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 82
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 1

`Art 82(2) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 82
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 2

`Art 82(3) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 82
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 3

`Art 82(4) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 82
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 4

`Art 82(5) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 82
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 5

`Art 83(1) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 83
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 1

`Art 83(2) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 83
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 2

§ `Article 82: the parties and the acts`

DECLARE `Art 82 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 82 the market surveillance authority`
    `Art 82 the Commission`
    `Art 82 a Member State`
    `Art 82 the provider or other relevant operator`

DECLARE `Art 82 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 82(1) require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures so that the AI system concerned no longer presents the risk`
    `Art 82(2) ensure that corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned made available on the Union market`
    `Art 82(3) inform the Commission and the other Member States of the finding`
    `Art 82(4) enter into consultation with the Member States concerned and the relevant operators and evaluate the national measures`
    `Art 82(4) decide whether the measure is justified`
    `Art 82(5) communicate the decision to the Member States concerned and to the relevant operators and inform the other Member States`

§ `Article 82(1): the market surveillance authority requires the operator to take measures`

-- src:1331 | 1. Where, having performed an evaluation under Article 79, after consulting the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1), the market surveillance authority of a Member State finds that although a high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation, it nevertheless presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection, it shall require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures to ensure that the AI system concerned, when placed on the market or put into service, no longer presents that risk without undue delay, within a period it may prescribe.
@ref Art 82(1) (src:1331)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has consulted the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 82(1) the market surveillance authority must require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 82(1) reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) as amended: "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply"); this provision is not among them (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE IF `the AI system`'s `route` EQUALS `Route neither`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is about "a high-risk AI system", and the AI system is not high-risk (a scope limit with no "only": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)
              ELSE IF       `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk`
                        AND `the market surveillance authority has consulted the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1)`
                        AND `the high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation`
                        AND `the AI system presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection`
                   THEN JUST TRUE  -- "without undue delay, within a period it may prescribe": the period is the authority's (input of paragraph 2)
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, having performed an evaluation under Article 79, after consulting the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1), the market surveillance authority of a Member State finds that although a high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation, it nevertheless presents a risk" (a "where" condition that is not met)

@ref Art 82(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has consulted the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 82 party` `Art 82 act`
`Art 82(1) the duty of the market surveillance authority to require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 82(1) the market surveillance authority must require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk` `the market surveillance authority has consulted the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1)` `the high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation` `the AI system presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 82 the market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 82(1) require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures so that the AI system concerned no longer presents the risk`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 82(2): the provider or other relevant operator ensures corrective action within the timeline`

-- src:1332 | 2. The provider or other relevant operator shall ensure that corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned that it has made available on the Union market within the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority of the Member State referred to in paragraph 1.
@ref Art 82(2) (src:1332)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has required the operator to take measures under Article 82(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the AI systems concerned that the operator has made available on the Union market` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those AI systems in respect of which corrective action has been taken within the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 82(2) the provider or other relevant operator has ensured that corrective action is taken` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 82(2) reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) as amended: "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply"); this provision is not among them (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE IF NOT `the market surveillance authority has required the operator to take measures under Article 82(1)`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority ... referred to in paragraph 1" exists only once the authority has acted under paragraph 1
              ELSE IF `the number of those AI systems in respect of which corrective action has been taken within the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority` AT LEAST `the number of the AI systems concerned that the operator has made available on the Union market`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provider or other relevant operator shall ensure that corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned that it has made available on the Union market within the timeline prescribed" (a bare "shall" not done: taken case by case, fork F-bare-must)

-- The deadline is the timeline the authority prescribes ("within a period it may prescribe", paragraph 1).
@ref Art 82(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has required the operator to take measures under Article 82(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority began` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 82 party` `Art 82 act`
`Art 82(2) the duty of the provider or other relevant operator to ensure corrective action` MEANS
    IF       `Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`
         AND NOT (`Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 82(2) reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE)  -- Article 2(2): this Article is not among those that apply to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach); the other answers leave the duty to its own provision
         AND `the market surveillance authority has required the operator to take measures under Article 82(1)`
    THEN PARTY `Art 82 the provider or other relevant operator`
         MUST `Art 82(2) ensure that corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned made available on the Union market`
         WITHIN (Day `the day on which the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority ends`) MINUS (Day `the day on which the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority began`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 82 the provider or other relevant operator` BECAUSE "corrective action was not taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned within the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

