    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 82(3) reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) as amended: "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply"); this provision is not among them (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE IF `the Member State has made a finding under Article 82(1)`
