`Art 83(1) the market surveillance authority must require the relevant provider to put an end to the non-compliance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 83(1) reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) as amended: "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply"); this provision is not among them (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE IF       `the market surveillance authority finds that the CE marking has been affixed in violation of Article 48`
                    OR `the market surveillance authority finds that the CE marking has not been affixed`
                    OR `the market surveillance authority finds that the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 has not been drawn up`
                    OR `the market surveillance authority finds that the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 has not been drawn up correctly`
                    OR `the market surveillance authority finds that the registration in the EU database referred to in Article 71 has not been carried out`
                    OR `the market surveillance authority finds that no authorised representative has been appointed, where applicable`
                    OR `the market surveillance authority finds that technical documentation is not available`
              THEN JUST TRUE  -- "within a period it may prescribe": the period is the authority's
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the market surveillance authority of a Member State makes one of the following findings" (a "where" condition that is not met; the list of findings (a) to (g) is introduced by "one of the following")

@ref Art 83(1)
